Cheshire East Council intends to procure a framework to fulfil its Domestic Build Works requirements for disability adaptations. This will assist Cheshire East Council in the completion of works in order to support vulnerable residents to help them to live safely and independently.

It is envisaged that our requirements will be split into two lots:

• Lot 1 - Building alterations

• Lot 2 - External works

Works that are required as part of this framework include the full range of domestic building works, including, but not limited to:

Lot 1

• Site Preparation;

• Foundations;

• External Walls and Insulation;

• Roofs and Insulation;

• Doors and Windows;

• Floors and Insulation;

• Internal walls and ceilings;

• Electrics;

• Plumbing and Drainage;

• Heating;

• Kitchens;

• Bathrooms.

Lot 2

• Ground Works;

• Fencing;

• External handrails;

• External Doors.

Cwm Taf Morgannwg UHB intend to award a contract to Honeywell Building Solutions, via a direct award under Sections 41-43 and Schedule 5 of the Procurement Act 2023, based on:

• Exclusive technical and IP capability;

• Critical urgency to safeguard patient care and operational integrity;

• Compliance with statutory and governance obligations;

• Demonstrated value for money and sustainability outcomes.

Given the proprietary nature of the existing system, the urgent need to maintain critical hospital services, and the exclusive technical capability of Honeywell, it is appropriate and compliant under the Procurement Act 2023 for this contract to be awarded directly to Honeywell Building Solutions.

This tender notice is for the award of a public contract through an open procedure in accordance with section 20(1) and (2)(a) of the PA 2023.

The Department for Infrastructure - Transport and Road Asset Management (TRAM) intends to establish a multi-contractor, multi-lot framework, for the delivery of Surface Dressing.

The Framework will include the following work activities: application of surface dressing, associated road markings, delivery of temporary traffic management as part of associated civils works on live trafficked public roads, and other associated ancillary works.

The Framework will comprise of seven Area Lots (1-7). A Measured Term Contract (MTC) Call-Off will be awarded for each Area Lot as listed below. Each MTC will deliver surface dressing works commissioned through Works Orders, each with a value of up to £750k.

Area Lots are:

SDF S2 - Newry, Mourne and Down / Ards and North Down;

SDF W2 - Derry and Strabane / Fermanagh and Omagh;

SDF S1 - Armagh, Banbridge and Craigavon;

SDF W1 - Mid Ulster;

SDF N1 - Causeway Coast and Glens;

SDF N2 - Mid and East Antrim / Antrim and Newtownabbey;

SDF E1 - Belfast / Lisburn and Castlereagh.

Framework award is expected to be in April 2026. However, works under the MTC Call-Off Contracts are not anticipated to commence until the 2027 Surface Dressing season, likely to commence in May 2027.

This Framework will deliver works from Call-Off contracts with an overall cumulative value of £80m (ex VAT) over the four year term. If the Contracting Authority is unable, for any reason, to award a new framework or to put in place an alternative regime to replace this Framework on its termination or expiry, any Call-Off Contract established under the Framework may be extended for a further period or periods up to a maximum of 12 additional months. This may increase the overall cumulative value to £100m (ex VAT).

The purpose of this Procurement Exercise is for:

An energy dispersive X-ray fluorescence spectrometer for reliable non-contact and non-destructive elemental analysis and mapping of heritage materials, with warranty as detailed in Section 3. The system should also function as a hand-held instrument and possess robust imaging capabilities, enabling comprehensive analysis and precise examination of materials.

The product(s) must come with user friendly software for measurement and data analysis (including all required licences, for up to 5 users) to control the system, to produce and manipulate images, and to analyse the data.

The Appointed Supplier must also:

deliver, set up, calibrate and test the system and software;

provide training to TNA staff in the use of the MA-XRF system and software within 2 months of delivery;

provide technical and/or remote support to TNA staff in the use of the MA-XRF and software for at least 5 years after delivery;

provide software upgrades for at least 3 years after purchase.

